{"name":"Nautical Star","hex":"#aab5b7","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"nautical star","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A symbol representing the North Star, associated with the sea services of the United States military, and indicating geographic north in compass roses on nautical charts."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nautical_star"}],"entries":[{"title":"Nautical star","blocks":[{"text":"The nautical star is a symbolic star representing the North Star, associated with the sea services of the United States armed forces and with tattoo culture. It is usually rendered as a five-pointed star in dark and light shades counterchanged in a style similar to a compass rose."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Nautical_star.svg/330px-Nautical_star.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nautical_star"},{"title":"Seamanship","blocks":[{"text":"Seamanship is the art, competence, and knowledge of operating a ship, boat or other craft on water. The Oxford Dictionary states that seamanship is \"The skill, techniques, or practice of handling a ship or boat at sea.\""}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/Seamanship_Centre_-_geograph.org.uk_-_943552.jpg/330px-Seamanship_Centre_-_geograph.org.uk_-_943552.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seamanship"},{"title":"Star","blocks":[{"text":"A star is a luminous spheroid of plasma held together by self-gravity. The nearest star to Earth is the Sun. Many other stars are visible to the naked eye at night; their immense distances from Earth make them appear as fixed points of light. The most prominent stars have been categorised into constellations and asterisms, and many of the brightest stars have proper names. Astronomers have assembled star catalogues that identify the known stars and provide standardized stellar designations. The observable universe contains an estimated 1022 to 1024 stars. Only about 4,000 of these stars are visible to the naked eye—all within the Milky Way galaxy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/The_Sun_in_white_light.jpg/330px-The_Sun_in_white_light.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Star"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Nautical_star.jpg/250px-Nautical_star.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/c6/Nautical_star.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Nautical_star.jpg/250px-Nautical_star.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A blue five-pointed nautical star wrist tattoo","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANautical_star.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Cargo_ship_being_loaded_%282929265311%29.jpg/500px-Cargo_ship_being_loaded_%282929265311%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Cargo_ship_being_loaded_%282929265311%29.jpg/1280px-Cargo_ship_being_loaded_%282929265311%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Cargo_ship_being_loaded_%282929265311%29.jpg/500px-Cargo_ship_being_loaded_%282929265311%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Seamanship involves loading cargo, calculating its effect on ship stability and ensuring it is correctly stowed and secured, such as on this car carrier.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/